          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1978205221,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I think your change to the template file is fine (I agree with Stig that it'd be nice to include a #define for the other port, even if we don't currently register for it).  Does your change need anything more than that (e.g., different .asn file versions, changes to its.cnf, even custom modifications to asn2wrs.py) ?\n\nOnce inputs are set correctly, you just need to build (make/ninja) in <build>/epan/dissectors/asn1/its, which will run the python script with ASN.1 files, the template you already edited and the conformance file (its.cnf).  If your change is rebased to current master, there should be very few changes to epan/dissectors/packet-its.c.  I'd expect to see clearly see the lines you changed, and not much more.  You won't find that it'll generate the exact version of packet-its.c that you were previously using - the code generation has been changed in several ways since it was generated.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
